  "name": "Send new-lead alerts, a 30-minute reminder and a daily summary with Gmail and Data Tables",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "80956e3b-bada-4d89-8b06-5d6081b47505",
      "name": "Template description",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 1,
        "width": 560,
        "height": 1060,
        "content": "## Send new-lead alerts, a 30-minute reminder and a daily summary with Gmail and Data Tables\n\n### Who's it for\nSmall businesses and teams whose website leads sometimes wait hours for a first answer, and who want one clear alert per lead instead of a busy inbox.\n\n### How it works\n1. Your form posts each lead (name, email, phone, message, source) to the webhook.\n2. The lead is cleaned up and given a key: a hash of the email or phone. If the same person already arrived within the repeat window, nothing happens.\n3. A new lead is stored in a data table and the owner gets one Gmail alert with a \"mark as answered\" link.\n4. If nobody opens that link within the reminder time, one reminder is sent. There is never a second one.\n5. Every evening a short email counts the day: received, answered in time, still open.\n\n### How to set up\n1. Create a data table with the columns **lead_key, name, email, phone, source** (text) and **received_at, answered_at, reminded_at** (date). Select it in the five Data table nodes.\n2. Connect your Gmail account in the three Gmail nodes.\n3. Fill in **Your settings**: owner email, reminder minutes, repeat window in days, timezone.\n4. Point your form at the webhook's production URL, then activate the workflow.\n\n### Requirements\n- n8n with Data tables\n- A Gmail account\n\n### How to customize the workflow\n- Swap the Gmail nodes for Slack, Telegram or Outlook.\n- Change the summary time in **Every evening at 20:00** and set the same timezone in the workflow settings.\n- Add Header Auth to the webhook if your form can send a header.\n\nMade by Betterlane \u2014 step-by-step guide: https://betterlaneagency.com/learn/n8n-workflow-runs-twice"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "6b9742f6-82aa-49c0-8bbc-87e2e58ceafa",
      "name": "Step 1 note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1260,
        60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 900,
        "height": 480,
        "content": "## 1. A lead arrives and is stored once\nThe webhook answers the form at once. The lead key is a hash, so a repeat within the window is recognised without using the contact as the key."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "3fdd93b2-6226-4b3a-a3b9-006cc976f00c",
      "name": "Step 2 note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2180,
        140
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1100,
        "height": 540,
        "content": "## 2. One alert, one reminder\nThe alert carries a private link. Opening it resumes this run and records the answer time. If the time limit passes first, one reminder goes out."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "6da631c2-400d-413e-a94e-829d394eb440",
      "name": "Step 3 note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1260,
        580
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 700,
        "height": 360,
        "content": "## 3. The daily summary\nEvery evening the day's rows are counted from the data table and emailed to the owner, even on a day with no leads."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
